---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { me } from '../../../data.js';

const title = 'GrammarLens terms of use';
const description = 'The terms that apply when you use GrammarLens.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Terms</strong>
      GrammarLens for iOS<br />
      Draft — not in force
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h1 class="display">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This address is reserved for the GrammarLens terms of use. The text is still being written.
        Nothing on this page is in force yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions in the meantime: <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a>
      </p>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Must be finished before the App Store submission.</strong> Apple requires a
          terms-of-use link for apps with auto-renewing subscriptions, and the review team opens this
          URL. The address itself is final — only the text below changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>01</strong>
      Who provides<br />
      the service
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>The agreement</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          State who provides the app (individual developer, Istanbul, no company), that installing or
          using the app means accepting these terms, and that the agreement is between the user and
          you — not Apple.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>02</strong>
      What you may<br />
      do with the app
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Licence</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          Describe the licence: personal, non-transferable, for use on devices the user owns. State
          what is not allowed — reselling access, automating requests, using the app as a proxy to
          the underlying API.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>03</strong>
      Subscriptions<br />
      and billing
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Paid features</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          The section Apple reads most closely. Cover: what the free tier includes, what the
          subscription unlocks, the billing period, that payment is charged to the Apple ID, that it
          renews automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the period ends, and that
          cancellation is done in App Store settings. Refunds are handled by Apple, not by you.
          Every claim here must match the App Store Connect product setup exactly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>04</strong>
      Accuracy of<br />
      the output
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>What the app does not promise</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          State plainly that explanations are produced by a language model and can be wrong, and that
          the app is a practice tool rather than certified exam preparation or professional language
          instruction. Write this honestly, not as a wall of disclaimers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>05</strong>
      Your text
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>The sentences you enter</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          Confirm the user keeps ownership of what they write, and point to the privacy policy for
          where that text goes. Keep this section consistent with section 03 of the privacy policy —
          if the two pages disagree, that is a review risk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>06</strong>
      Availability,<br />
      changes, ending
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Changes and termination</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          Cover: the service may be interrupted or discontinued, terms may change with notice on this
          page, and either side may end the agreement — the user by deleting the app. Add the
          governing law (Turkey) and a contact address for disputes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>07</strong>
      Contact
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a> with anything about these terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/privacy">Privacy policy</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/support">Support page</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/products/grammarlens">GrammarLens</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
